OTP 25
=== A: user type with a built-in's name, default options
t1.erl:3:2: type map() is a builtin type; it cannot be redefined
%    3| -type map() :: {my, map}.          % redefine built-in map/0
%     |  ^

exit=1
=== B: same, with -compile(no_auto_import_types).  READ: it compiles, but lint says the user type is UNUSED although -spec f(map()) uses the name => the use site still resolved to the built-in (declaration allowed, shadowing not achieved).  Inference from the warning, not a separate test.
t2.erl:4:2: Warning: type map() is unused
%    4| -type map() :: {my, map}.          % redefine built-in map/0
%     |  ^

exit=0
=== C: a type that is NOT built in (control, must compile)
exit=0
=== D: the same type name twice (control: the other error class, redefine_type)
t4.erl:4:2: type mymap() already defined
%    4| -type mymap() :: b.
%     |  ^

t4.erl:3:2: Warning: type mymap() is unused
%    3| -type mymap() :: a.
%     |  ^

exit=1
